title: "lidar-terrain-arcgis-tools: ArcGIS Pro toolbox for LiDAR-derived topographic factors"
abstract: >-
  An ArcGIS Pro Python toolbox that derives topographic factors from DGT LiDAR elevation data
  (DEM and DSM) in batch, per area of interest. It downloads the elevation tiles and the
  orthophotos from the DGT CDD portal (mainland Portugal and the Azores), builds per area and
  per cluster mosaics, derives slope, aspect, hillshade and curvature, computes annual solar
  radiation with the GPU RasterSolarRadiation tool, reclassifies aspect, slope and solar into
  suitability classes, resamples, merges and vectorizes the outputs, and builds orthophoto
  mosaics. Mosaics keep the CRS of their tiles: EPSG:3763 (ETRS89 / PT-TM06) on the mainland,
  UTM zone 25N or 26N (PTRA08) in the Azores.
